## Architecture Notes

### Domain-Driven Design

This API follows a DDD architecture pattern:

```
app/
├── Domain/                    # Domain Layer
│   ├── [Entity]/              # e.g., Usuario, Conjunto
│   │   ├── Entities/          # Domain entities
│   │   ├── Repositories/      # Repository interfaces
│   │   └── ValueObjects/      # Value objects
│   └── Common/Exceptions/     # Shared exceptions
├── Application/               # Application Layer
│   └── [Entity]/              # e.g., Usuario
│       ├── DTOs/              # Data Transfer Objects
│       └── Handlers/          # Command/Query handlers
├── Http/
│   ├── Controllers/Api/       # API Controllers
│   ├── Requests/              # Form Request validation
│   └── Resources/             # API Resources
└── Models/                    # Eloquent Models (legacy/Reliese)
```

### Controller Pattern

All API controllers follow this pattern:
1. Validate request with Form Request class
2. Delegate to Application Handler
3. Return API Resource wrapped response
4. Use standard HTTP status codes

### Response Wrapping

- Single resource: `UsuarioResource::make($entity)->response()`
- Collection: `UsuarioResource::collection($paginator)->response()`
- Creates: HTTP 201 with resource
- Updates: HTTP 200 with resource
- Deletes: HTTP 204 No Content

